# 9. API Requirements

The following APIs are currently implemented:

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/events` | Retrieve all events |
| GET | `/api/events/:id` | Retrieve one event |
| GET | `/api/bookings` | Retrieve bookings |
| GET | `/api/bookings/:id` | Retrieve booking by ID |
| POST | `/api/bookings` | Create a booking |
| GET | `/api/contacts` | Retrieve contact messages |
| POST | `/api/contacts` | Submit contact message |
| GET | `/health` | Check backend status |

---

# 10. Contact Management

The system shall allow users to submit contact messages.

The following information shall be validated:

- Name
- Email
- Message

The email must have a valid email format.

Empty names or messages shall be rejected.

---

# 11. Database Requirements

The current database contains the following core tables:

## Users

Stores user information such as:

- ID
- Name
- Email
- Phone
- Created date

## Events

Stores:

- Event ID
- Event name
- Description
- Venue ID
- Event date
- Event time
- Price
- Image URL
- Available tickets

## Bookings

Stores booking-related information such as:

- Booking ID
- User ID
- Event ID
- Number of tickets
- Total amount
- Booking date
- Booking status

## Venues

Stores venue-related information.

## Tickets

Stores ticket-related information.

## Contacts

Stores contact form submissions.

